git apply philosophy-5-values.patchdiff --git a/changelog.html b/changelog.html
index c5d864b..a1c5b65 100644
--- a/changelog.html
+++ b/changelog.html
@@ -12,6 +12,15 @@
     <div class="main-container">
         <h1>Changelog</h1>
 
+        <div class="description-box">
+            <h3>3.14.2 - 22.11.2026</h3>
+            <ul>
+                <li>5 philosophy values are added, each with an AI-made icon (marked as such on its page) and a definition: Historical Materialism, Absolute Idealism, Actual Idealism, Positivism and Thomism. There are now 15 philosophy values and 165 values in all.</li>
+                <li>Materialism and idealism now each open a follow-up question. Materialism splits into plain materialism and Historical Materialism; idealism splits into plain idealism, Absolute Idealism (Hegel) and Actual Idealism (Gentile). Positivism is a new option under "How do you decide whether a claim is true?" and Thomism under the question about weighing a promise against a larger good.</li>
+                <li>The new values have estimated stances on the ideologies (Historical Materialism 68, Absolute Idealism 70, Actual Idealism 19, Positivism 75, Thomism 90), set from each ideology's existing philosophy stances, its group and the values it already holds, with named corrections for the clear cases such as Marxism and Italian Fascism. Only stances of 0.3 or more in either direction are listed, because every listed stance slightly lowers an ideology's rank for answers that do not use it. For the 538 value sets that define the ideologies, the best match is the same as before for 470, and the share that rank first for their own defining values went from 218 to 206.</li>
+            </ul>
+        </div>
+
         <div class="description-box">
             <h3>3.13.3 - 21.11.2026</h3>
             <ul>
