     "Anarcho-Fascism": {
         "d": "A decentralist doctrine from Jonas Nilsson's book Anarcho-Fascism: Nature Reborn (2017): government authority should be practiced in the smallest possible units able to keep their own sovereignty, beginning with the family, whose head is its authority both inside and out, and defended by a generally armed population and local militias instead of a central army or bureaucracy (patchwork, subsidiarity and confederalism, with centralism and hypercentralism rejected). The state exists only to defend its people in war and to help them flourish, and it serves the interests of its own kin and in-group (tribalism, ethnic nationalism and communitarianism) within a shared Western civilization (civilizationism) and an armed neutrality abroad. It holds that falsehoods contrary to nature, such as feminism and universal human rights, are the cause of Western decline, and it calls for a traditional, family-centered and masculine order (traditionalist conservatism and reactionaryism). It rejects cosmopolitanism, globalism, multiculturalism, progressivism, social progressivism and civil liberalism.",
